# Secrets / moat / memory protection (NO EXCEPTIONS)

**Locked 2026-09-04.** Agents must keep sensitive material out of git remotes and tracked public docs.

## Never `git add` / commit / push

| Path / class | Why |
|--------------|-----|
| `src/moat/`, `assets/moat/`, API moat adapters | Proprietary product |
| `.brain/` (MindLink) | Session/ops/moat memory |
| `memory-bank/` | Protected state / strategy |
| `.sessionmem-team/` | Team memory dumps |
| `.env`, `.env.*` (except `*.example`) | Secrets |
| `.cursor/mcp.json` | May embed API keys |
| `MONETIZATION_ROADMAP.md`, `FUTURE_RD.md`, API root `MESH_WRAP_ROADMAP.md`, `Pitch Deck/` | Strategy / moat |
| `scripts/staging-*/` (live-speech / avatar staging helpers), `scripts/tmp-*`, `docs/restore-points/`, `*.bak` | Scratch / moat restore overlays |
| `*.pem`, `*.key`, `secrets/`, `credentials.json` | Crypto material |

## SessionMem / MindLink content

- **Load** at startup (continuity rules). **Do not** paste secrets, API keys, wallet private keys, or moat vendor filenames into tracked `.mdc` / README / public docs.
- Prefer `storeMemory` + `.brain/` / `memory-bank/` (gitignored) for sensitive decisions.
- Public-safe process only belongs in alwaysApply rules.

## Sync vs git

- DGX → Surface `sync-changes-to-pc.sh --include-src` may copy **moat** for local Surface work — that is **not** a GitHub publish.
- Sync must **not** push `.brain/`, `.sessionmem-team/`, `.env`, or `.cursor/mcp.json` (blocked in `sync-changes-lib.sh`).
- `memory-bank/` / `graphify-out/` only with `--include-agent-context` (still local machines, not remotes).

## Remotes

- Do **not** `git push` unless the user explicitly orders a specific push in that turn (`spacetime-moat-protected.mdc`).
- If a secret was ever committed historically, stop and tell the user to rotate — do not silently re-commit.

## Pre-commit

OpenNexus: `scripts/pre-commit-block-secrets.sh` via `.git/hooks/pre-commit`. Keep it installed; do not `--no-verify`.
